# Offline pin notes — gpw-hirshfeld-uks-kpoints

## Method

Hirshfeld \(V/V_{\mathrm{free}}\) from the **multi-k collinear UKS** GPW PBE
total valence density \(\rho=\sum_k w_k(\rho_k^\alpha+\rho_k^\beta)\) (in-tree
exponential free-atom model, `hirshfeld_tables.h`) → MBD@rsSCS with scaled
α/C6/R (same libMBD free-atom tables as `gpw-mbd-ice` / `gpw-hirshfeld-uks` /
`gpw-hirshfeld-kpoints`). Product path: `fold_dispersion_k_uks` in
`gpw_solver.cpp`.

## Why not stock CP2K QS?

CP2K 2026.1 `PAIR_POTENTIAL TYPE` is only DFTD2|DFTD3|DFTD3(BJ)|DFTD4 — no
stock TS/MBD. Hard pin is the ATV product under fixed multi-k UKS settings
(CUTOFF 120 Ry, DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH, GTH-PBE-q6, O₂ triplet Nα=7/Nβ=5,
periodic 10 Å, Monkhorst–Pack 2×2×1 + TR), cross-checked vs free-atom MBD on
the same geometry and the dual in-tree Hirshfeld kernel.

**Binary checked (host, not a twin):** `source
/nobackup/proj/disk/teoroo/personal/jicli594/work/cp2k/install/env.sh` →
`cp2k.psmp` **2026.1** `git:5e54ba2` (capability confirmation only — no
TS/MBD output line to pin against).

## Geometry

Centered O₂ R = 1.2075 Å in 10 Å cubic periodic cell (same bond length as
`gpw-uks-pbe` / `gpw-hirshfeld-uks`; smaller cell than Γ-UKS MT for multi-k
wall).

## Pin (product settings)

```
E_disp = -1.0427466367435301e-04 Ha
free-atom MBD dual (v=1, same geom) = -1.1699749375715385e-04 Ha
volumes (O O) ≈ 0.6823 0.6823
CUTOFF 120 Ry, k-mesh 2×2×1 TR (n_kpts=2), DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH, GTH-PBE-q6
O2 triplet Nα=7/Nβ=5, periodic 10 Å, max_iter 80, tol 1e-6, mix 0.45
```

